    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0411" n="337" xml:id="pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">W.P.B. Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister of Supply</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Beaverbrook</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Vice President</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-29">December 29,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Vice-President</hi>: I enclose you copies of
                    a letter and two documents sent to the President by me.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d192-f1"/></p>
                <p>The first document was sent on the 27th of December and the second document on
                    the 29th of December.</p>
                <p>If I can answer any questions, will you please let me know?</p>
                <p>I am most grateful for all the time you gave today and the patience you
                    displayed.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaverbrook</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d192-f1" n="1" xml:id="d192-f1-content">
                <p>The enclosures were copies of Beaverbrook’s letter to Roosevelt, dated December
                    27, 1941 (<hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg328">p. 328</ref>),
                    Beaverbrook’s memorandum enclosed with that letter (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg329">p. 329</ref>), and Beaverbrook’s memorandum
                    for Roosevelt of December 29 (<hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg334">p. 334</ref>).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
